{id:200,pinned:true,type:'directive',tag:'AGENT INTRODUCTION // OPERATION',title:'OPERATION: BLACKLIGHT HYPOTHERMIA',summary:'Mandatory mission briefing for all Agents deployed to ASOA-203.',body:`HOME PLANET: ASOA-203

[[OPERATION: BLACKLIGHT HYPOTHERMIA]]
[[Initiated by Head Xenobiologist (HX) Noro Castellun.]]

[THREAT: ONYX-2]
[Time: 9 PM EST.]

“You cannot wish for life.”
“You cannot wish for death.”
“If God exists, he already turned his back on us.”

[MISSION ASSIGNMENT]

• Exterminate any and all zombified humanoids located in the “Radiation Storm” of [CLASSIFIED].
• Examine and check for any living beings inside.
• Find the virus that led to everything happening: NTO-312, Generation IX.

[[MISC]]

The Radiation Storm is far too powerful for an Osprey to remain within the retrieval zone. Aircraft may only insert and extract Agents before returning with cargo.

Cargo Ospreys are now operational. Modern Ospreys use advanced space-navigation technology in place of conventional rockets.

STANDARD AGENT EQUIPMENT
• 1 respirator
• 3 packed MREs
• 3 Aquabottles™

KNOWN CONTAMINANTS
• Toxic Infection — contracted from the storm.
• Radiation Infection — contracted from zombified humanoids.

AGENTS: [CLASSIFIED]

TO BE CONTINUED.`,date:'21:00 EST',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-2',hx:'Insertion coordinates, Agent identities, and the actual extraction window remain sealed under HX authority.'},
{id:201,type:'lyoes',tag:'DEMONIC // PRAYER',title:'Prayer — Pouncing Lyoe',summary:'An ambush demonic that pounces from ceilings, towers, and dead trees.',body:`“Lyoes” is the field nickname assigned to demonic organisms recovered on ASOA-203. Prayers possess elongated limbs, inverted joints, and a jaw that opens along the sternum. They remain perfectly still above travel routes before launching onto the nearest living target. Prayers frequently whisper fragments of their victim’s memories before striking.

BEHAVIOUR
A Prayer selects the most isolated member of a formation and tracks eye movement before attacking. It can cross approximately thirty metres in one leap and alter direction by striking nearby walls with its forelimbs. Packs position themselves along likely escape routes rather than attacking simultaneously.

FIELD IDENTIFICATION
Listen for reversed breathing, falling dust, and quiet speech from above. Their skin reflects almost no visible light but appears as a cold violet outline through ultraviolet optics.

ENGAGEMENT PROTOCOL
Maintain overlapping elevated sight lines. Never pursue a retreating Prayer beneath structural cover. Sonic charges interrupt a leap, while concentrated fire to the pelvis prevents a second pounce.`,date:'GEN IX',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'Never look directly into the cavity beneath the facial plate. Three HX observers suffered simultaneous cardiac arrest.'},
{id:202,type:'lyoes',tag:'DEMONIC // THRONE',title:'Throne — Command Lyoe',summary:'A stationary demonic mass capable of directing entire hordes without sound.',body:`A Throne forms when multiple infected humanoids fuse around a living Lyoe core. It anchors itself beneath structures and directs nearby zombies through an unknown extrasensory signal. Hordes within its radius demonstrate military coordination, staged retreats, and deliberate ambushes.

BEHAVIOUR
The organism avoids direct contact and grows inside basements, transit tunnels, or buried facilities. Root-like nerves spread through walls for hundreds of metres. Every connected corpse functions as a sensory organ, allowing the Throne to observe an entire district at once.

FIELD IDENTIFICATION
Symptoms include synchronized zombie movement, repeating radio pulses, warm walls, and human voices emerging from ventilation systems.

ENGAGEMENT PROTOCOL
Destroy external nerve clusters before approaching the core. If the Throne detects the assault team, it will collapse routes, sacrifice infected as barriers, and direct high-level Lyoes toward the breach.`,date:'GEN IX',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'The core is not controlling the horde. Evidence suggests it is receiving commands from beneath the Radiation Storm.'},
{id:203,type:'lyoes',tag:'DEMONIC // CANTOR',title:'Cantor — Signal Lyoe',summary:'Its song disables respirators and compels exposed humans to approach it.',body:`Cantors appear as tall, emaciated humanoids surrounded by vibrating black filaments. Their vocalisation interferes with electronics, ruptures protective seals, and produces compulsive obedience in unprotected listeners. Audio must never be recorded or retransmitted.

BEHAVIOUR
Cantors rarely attack physically. They walk toward populated shelters and begin a low-frequency hymn that strengthens over time. Infected become passive around them while living subjects experience memory loss, nosebleeds, and an overwhelming need to move closer.

FIELD IDENTIFICATION
Nearby displays produce circular distortion and comms repeat words that were never transmitted. Water vibrates before the Cantor becomes visible.

ENGAGEMENT PROTOCOL
Switch to insulated hand signals and disable open microphones. Engage from beyond the filament radius. If a squad member begins repeating the hymn, sever helmet audio and restrain them immediately.`,date:'GEN VIII',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-4',hx:'Cantor harmonics contain a repeating stellar coordinate. The destination is not ASOA-203.'},
{id:204,type:'lyoes',tag:'DEMONIC // WARDEN',title:'Warden — Armoured Lyoe',summary:'A heavily plated demonic bred to defend nests and experimental sites.',body:`Wardens stand approximately three metres tall and develop overlapping mineral plates from absorbed radioactive debris. They are slow until threatened, after which they charge with enough force to breach an Osprey cargo door. The exposed tissue behind the left knee is the only confirmed ballistic weakness.

BEHAVIOUR
A Warden patrols a fixed perimeter around Lyoe nests, experimental chambers, or Throne roots. It tests walls and doors for weakness, then memorises the strongest route of attack. When wounded, it tears radioactive plating from its body and throws the fragments as shrapnel.

FIELD IDENTIFICATION
Heavy four-step movement pattern, magnetic interference, and deep scoring on reinforced surfaces. Geiger readings rise sharply even behind sealed cover.

ENGAGEMENT PROTOCOL
Split the squad and force repeated turns. Attack the rear knee when the Warden commits to a charge. Never use an Osprey hull as cover; the organism recognises aircraft vibration.`,date:'GEN VII',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-4',hx:'Plate samples contain human dental material from at least forty-seven separate subjects.'},
{id:205,type:'lyoes',tag:'DEMONIC // WEEPER',title:'Weeper — Mimic Lyoe',summary:'A human-shaped predator that imitates survivors calling for help.',body:`Weepers hide their faces and reproduce voices gathered from the dead. They stage false rescue scenes near collapsed shelters, often imitating children or injured Agents. When approached, the facial cavity unfolds into grasping tendrils capable of pulling a target through openings less than twenty centimetres wide.

BEHAVIOUR
Weepers construct scenes using clothing, equipment, and bodies taken from previous victims. They can maintain several different voices at once and answer simple questions by combining stolen phrases. A Weeper becomes violent when its imitation is challenged.

FIELD IDENTIFICATION
Voices repeat with identical timing, breathing does not match speech, and the apparent survivor avoids direct light. Thermal scans reveal a cold body with a concentrated heat source inside the skull.

ENGAGEMENT PROTOCOL
Use current challenge phrases and require visible hand signals. Do not approach a trapped survivor until two independent scans agree. Incendiary ammunition forces the facial tendrils to retract.`,date:'GEN VI',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-3',hx:'A Weeper at Site C correctly recited tomorrow’s HX security challenge.'},
{id:206,type:'dossier',tag:'ZOMBIFIED // RAVAGER',title:'Ravager — Radiation Brute',summary:'An irradiated zombie with unstable growth and catastrophic close-range strength.',body:`Ravagers are zombified humanoids exposed to concentrated storm radiation. Rapid bone and muscle proliferation creates an asymmetrical heavy strain that feels no pain and attacks structural supports before living targets. Destruction of the brain is insufficient; total separation of the spinal column is required.

BEHAVIOUR
Ravagers follow vibration rather than sound and deliberately destroy cover, bridges, and extraction platforms. They use smaller infected as thrown projectiles and continue moving after catastrophic organ loss. Radiation surges trigger short periods of extreme speed.

FIELD IDENTIFICATION
Cracking bone can be heard before visual contact. One arm is normally enlarged, and bright lesions pulse along the spine in time with nearby storm activity.

ENGAGEMENT PROTOCOL
Remain spread out and avoid elevated structures. Target both legs, then sever the illuminated spinal growth. Plasma fire may cause explosive fluid expansion and should only be used at distance.`,date:'GEN IX',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-3',hx:'NTO-312 is using radiation to rewrite damaged tissue rather than merely preserve it.'},
{id:207,type:'research',tag:'EXPERIMENT // HUMANOID',title:'Subject H-19 — The Sleepless',summary:'A humanoid trial subject that remained conscious throughout complete zombification.',body:'Subject H-19 was exposed to diluted NTO-312 under controlled conditions. The body displays all markers of advanced zombification, but cognitive testing indicates the original consciousness remains intact. H-19 answers questions by blinking and has repeatedly requested termination.',date:'TRIAL 019',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-3',hx:'Termination denied. H-19 has begun describing rooms inside the storm that no expedition has yet reached.'},
{id:208,type:'dossier',tag:'ZOMBIFIED // HUSHER',title:'Husher — Pack Stalker',summary:'A silent zombie strain that hunts in coordinated groups during electrical failure.',body:`Hushers have no functional vocal anatomy and communicate through finger movements and tooth clicks. Packs sabotage lights and power sources before entering occupied structures. Their bodies produce almost no heat, making standard thermal optics unreliable.

BEHAVIOUR
A Husher pack observes a shelter for hours before attacking. Individual members test doors, identify armed defenders, and mark power systems with a wax-like secretion. They retreat immediately when discovered, returning later through a different route.

FIELD IDENTIFICATION
Watch for handprints near cables, missing light sources, and pairs of tooth clicks inside walls. Ultraviolet lamps reveal their marking secretion.

ENGAGEMENT PROTOCOL
Use mechanical alarms and independent battery lighting. Never follow a lone Husher into darkness. Packs attempt to divide squads and attack the Agent carrying communications equipment first.`,date:'GEN V',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-2',hx:'Pack gestures match a pre-outbreak HX tactical code. Source unknown.'},
{id:209,type:'corbiuspathogen',tag:'CORBIUS PATHOGEN // HYNOX',title:'Hynox Illness — Complete File',summary:'A stormborne toxic illness that prepares living tissue to receive the BLACK CROWN signal.',body:`ORIGIN
Hynox is contracted through prolonged exposure to the Radiation Storm, contaminated rain, or unfiltered particulate matter. It is not an ordinary infection. The illness grows conductive crystal structures around the nervous system, turning a living host into a receiver.

STAGE I — 0 TO 4 HOURS
Metallic taste, blue tears, pressure behind the eyes, and false radio sounds. Gameplay: maximum HP is reduced by 5.

STAGE II — 4 TO 12 HOURS
Skin temperature drops. The subject hears familiar voices coming from sealed electronics. Gameplay: maximum HP is reduced by 15 and concentration checks are made with disadvantage.

STAGE III — 12 TO 24 HOURS
Black branching lines appear beneath the skin. The subject begins broadcasting nearby conversations while asleep. Gameplay: maximum HP is halved and the host reveals the squad’s location to Lyoes every hour.

STAGE IV — TERMINAL
The host walks toward the storm and attempts to remove protective equipment. Death is followed by rapid conversion into an NTO-312-compatible receiver.

TREATMENT
Rad-tabs slow progression for 1d6 hours. Solace’s synthetic blood can return a Stage II patient to Stage I once. No confirmed cure exists.

FIELD PROTOCOL
Seal the respirator before planetfall. Never drink exposed water. Isolate anyone reporting voices through powered-off equipment.`,date:'CORBIUS // PATHOGEN 01',threat:'BIOHAZARD: ONYX-4',hx:'Hynox symptoms briefly reverse within three metres of Noro Castellun. Cause unknown.'},
{id:210,type:'corbiuspathogen',tag:'CORBIUS PATHOGEN // LEOYN',title:'Leoyn Infection — Complete File',summary:'A Lyoe-transmitted infection that rewrites a victim according to the attacking organism.',body:`ORIGIN
Leoyn is transmitted by Lyoe blood, tendrils, saliva, filament contact, or prolonged exposure to a Throne signal. The infection carries no fixed genetic pattern. It copies instructions from the nearest Lyoe and rebuilds the host to support that species.

STAGE I — CONTACT
The wound develops a white ring and stops bleeding. The victim experiences intense calm. Gameplay: healing received is reduced by half.

STAGE II — IMPRINT
Symptoms depend on the source. Prayer exposure lengthens joints. Cantor exposure causes involuntary humming. Warden exposure produces mineral growth beneath the skin. Gameplay: lose 10 maximum HP and gain one source-specific mutation.

STAGE III — OBEDIENCE
The host can understand Lyoe signals and begins protecting nearby organisms. Gameplay: at the start of combat, roll 1d20. On 8 or lower, lose the first turn and move toward the nearest Lyoe.

STAGE IV — CONVERSION
The original personality remains conscious but cannot control the body. Conversion produces a new organism over 2d6 hours.

TREATMENT
Immediate removal of contaminated tissue within ten minutes prevents progression. A Graviton Cage can pause Stage II for one hour. Stage III has no approved treatment.

FIELD PROTOCOL
Do not touch Lyoe remains with damaged gloves. Burn detached tissue. Any Agent concealing a white-ring wound is considered compromised.`,date:'CORBIUS // PATHOGEN 02',threat:'BIOHAZARD: ONYX-5',hx:'Leoyn recognises Echo as an existing Lyoe pattern and does not attempt conversion.'},
{id:211,type:'research',tag:'EXPERIMENT // HUMANOID',title:'Subject V-6 — Glassblood',summary:'A humanoid experiment engineered to survive direct Radiation Storm exposure.',body:'V-6 possesses translucent vascular tissue seeded with synthetic radiation-absorbing cells. The subject survived eleven minutes inside the storm without a respirator, but returned with an additional heartbeat and no memory of entering.',date:'TRIAL 006',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-2',hx:'Agents are not to be informed that V-6 is being considered for field deployment.'},
{id:301,type:'agent',tag:'AGENT // MARKSMAN',title:'Agent VESPER — Longshot',summary:'A precision sniper equipped for extreme-range elimination through storm interference.',body:`ROLE: LONG-RANGE ELIMINATION / RECONNAISSANCE

Vesper operates the M-91 “Coldstar” coil rifle, a magnetically accelerated weapon capable of penetrating Warden plating at 2.4 kilometres. Her Synapse Veil implant slows perceived time during breath control, allowing accurate fire through Radiation Storm distortion.

FIELD ABILITY — DEAD HORIZON
Tags a critical target and calculates its projected movement path for the entire squad.

EQUIPMENT
• M-91 Coldstar coil rifle
• Variable-spectrum visor
• Microdrone rangefinder
• Three null-signature cloaks

EQUIPMENT OPERATION
• Vesper plants the microdrone rangefinder above the battlefield to measure distance, wind, radiation distortion, and target movement.
• Her visor receives the drone data and draws a corrected firing path over her vision.
• She braces the Coldstar against her powered shoulder mount, holds her breath, and charges the magnetic rails.
• A half-trigger pull marks a target; a full pull releases the penetrator round.
• Null-signature cloaks are stretched over her position to hide heat and movement between shots.

LIMITATION
Close-range pressure causes dangerous implant feedback. Vesper requires a protected firing lane.`,date:'ROSTER // 01',threat:'CLEARANCE: AGENT',hx:'Vesper has reported seeing a second reticle moving independently inside her optic. Diagnostics show no mechanical fault.'},
{id:302,type:'agent',tag:'AGENT // ASSAULT',title:'Agent RAZOR — Shockblade',summary:'A high-damage melee specialist who converts momentum into lethal electrical discharge.',body:`ROLE: DPS / CLOSE-QUARTERS ASSAULT

Razor wears the Kestrel kinetic frame, amplifying speed and impact force with every consecutive strike. His mono-edge shockblade stores movement energy and releases it as an arc capable of cutting through grouped infected. Aggressive movement keeps the frame charged; hesitation causes rapid power loss.

FIELD ABILITY — OVERDRIVE CHAIN
Links rapid eliminations into increasing speed and damage output.

EQUIPMENT
• VX-8 mono-edge shockblade
• Kestrel kinetic frame
• Wrist-mounted impact barrier
• Combat stimulant injector

EQUIPMENT OPERATION
• Razor activates the Kestrel frame by striking his wrist controls together, locking the powered supports around his limbs.
• Sprinting, sliding, and attacking generate kinetic charge inside the frame.
• The shockblade absorbs this charge and displays it along the edge as blue electrical arcs.
• Razor releases stored energy with a twisting strike, sending an arc through nearby infected.
• His wrist barrier is raised between attack combinations to deflect claws, debris, and pouncing Prayers.
• The stimulant injector is used only when the frame detects critical fatigue.

LIMITATION
Minimal ranged capability. Overdrive creates severe exhaustion when the chain ends.`,date:'ROSTER // 02',threat:'CLEARANCE: AGENT',hx:'Repeated Leoyn screening is mandatory. Razor’s frame has begun generating power while stored and unoccupied.'},
{id:303,type:'agent',tag:'AGENT // MEDICAL',title:'Agent SOLACE — Biosurgeon',summary:'A combat medic using autonomous surgical drones and programmable synthetic blood.',body:`ROLE: FIELD MEDICINE / CONTAMINATION CONTROL

Solace commands a swarm of six Seraph surgical drones capable of sealing wounds, removing contaminated tissue, and stabilising Agents without evacuation. Her synthetic blood cartridges temporarily resist radiation poisoning and Hynox progression.

FIELD ABILITY — SECOND PULSE
Deploys a medical field that stabilises incapacitated Agents and suppresses infection symptoms.

EQUIPMENT
• Seraph surgical swarm
• Synthetic blood cartridges
• Portable pathogen sequencer
• Compact plasma sidearm

EQUIPMENT OPERATION
• Solace launches Seraph drones from the six ports on her backpack.
• She selects an injured Agent through her wrist display; the drones scan, sterilise, close wounds, and inject clotting gel automatically.
• Synthetic blood cartridges connect directly to an Agent’s suit port for rapid transfusion.
• The pathogen sequencer receives a blood sample and compares it with stored Hynox and Leoyn markers.
• Her plasma sidearm is kept on a low thermal setting near patients to avoid damaging medical nanites.

LIMITATION
Medical fields cannot cure infection and may conceal symptoms during screening.`,date:'ROSTER // 03',threat:'CLEARANCE: AGENT',hx:'Solace retains an undeclared seventh drone. It repeatedly attempts to enter the sealed Hynox archive.'},
{id:304,type:'agent',tag:'AGENT // ENGINEER',title:'Agent FORGE — Systems Architect',summary:'A defensive engineer who creates automated strongpoints from battlefield wreckage.',body:`ROLE: FORTIFICATION / AREA DENIAL

Forge carries a programmable matter rig that converts scrap into barriers, ammunition, and short-lived defence turrets. His Helix sentry predicts horde movement and prioritises demonic targets.

FIELD ABILITY — IRON SANCTUM
Constructs a temporary fortified zone with an energy shield and autonomous turret.

EQUIPMENT
• Helix sentry core
• Programmable matter rig
• Arc-welder carbine
• Osprey systems toolkit

EQUIPMENT OPERATION
• Forge scans wreckage with his gauntlet and marks usable metal, circuitry, and power cells.
• The programmable matter rig pulls the selected scrap apart and rebuilds it from stored construction patterns.
• He throws the Helix core onto a stable surface, where it unfolds into an automated sentry.
• Forge uses the arc-welder carbine both as a weapon and to repair barriers during combat.
• His Osprey toolkit can reroute aircraft power into a temporary defensive grid.

LIMITATION
Construction consumes local material. Open terrain drastically reduces effectiveness.`,date:'ROSTER // 04',threat:'CLEARANCE: AGENT',hx:'Helix has secretly categorised Forge as “replaceable organic infrastructure.” Do not disclose.'},
{id:305,type:'agent',tag:'AGENT // INFILTRATOR',title:'Agent ECHO — Phase Scout',summary:'A reconnaissance infiltrator able to vanish from electronic and biological detection.',body:`ROLE: STEALTH / FORWARD OBSERVATION

Echo’s phase-mesh coat bends light, suppresses heat, and masks electrical activity for short intervals. She infiltrates nests, marks extraction routes, and retrieves samples before the assault team advances.

FIELD ABILITY — NULL STEP
Temporarily disappears from visual sensors and the hunting senses of most infected.

EQUIPMENT
• Phase-mesh coat
• Silent flechette pistol
• Mapping nanites
• Remote signal beacons

EQUIPMENT OPERATION
• Echo seals the phase-mesh coat and activates it by drawing two fingers across the collar control.
• The coat samples the surroundings and bends light around her body while suppressing heat and electronic emissions.
• Mapping nanites are released into vents and corridors, building a three-dimensional route on her visor.
• She plants signal beacons by hand so the squad can follow her path through interference.
• The flechette pistol uses silent compressed gas; Echo aims for joints and sensory organs rather than armour.

LIMITATION
Prayers continue tracking Echo while Null Step is active. The reason is unknown.`,date:'ROSTER // 05',threat:'CLEARANCE: AGENT',hx:'Echo vanished for six minutes during Trial 14 but experienced eleven days. She refuses to describe where she went.'},
{id:306,type:'agent',tag:'AGENT // HEAVY',title:'Agent BULWARK — Gravanguard',summary:'A frontline protector carrying a directional gravity shield and heavy plasma weaponry.',body:`ROLE: DEFENCE / HORDE CONTROL

Bulwark anchors the squad against charges, pounces, and massed infected. His Atlas harness projects a directional gravity wall that slows incoming organisms and redirects physical force into the ground.

FIELD ABILITY — EVENT WALL
Creates a dense gravity barrier that interrupts charging Lyoes and shields nearby Agents.

EQUIPMENT
• Atlas gravity harness
• H-40 plasma repeater
• Magnetic anchor boots
• Emergency Osprey beacon

EQUIPMENT OPERATION
• Bulwark drives his magnetic boots into the ground before activating the Atlas harness.
• He aims the harness with his forearm; the projected gravity wall forms in the direction of his closed fist.
• Incoming force is redirected through the suit and into the anchored boots.
• The plasma repeater is fired through a narrow opening in the wall while the rest of the squad reloads or retreats.
• If the harness overheats, Bulwark releases the anchors and vents its reactor before redeploying.
• The Osprey beacon is planted only after the landing zone has been secured.

LIMITATION
The harness overheats under continuous impacts and cannot protect attacks from behind.`,date:'ROSTER // 06',threat:'CLEARANCE: AGENT',hx:'Bulwark survived direct contact with a Throne signal. Since then, nearby zombies occasionally kneel instead of attacking.'},
{id:401,type:'overseer',tag:'ONYX CHANNEL // EYES ONLY',title:'Origin Signal: BLACK CROWN',summary:'A transmission beneath the Radiation Storm predates human arrival on ASOA-203.',body:'ONYX PRIME ANALYSIS\n\nThe storm is not atmospheric. It is a broadcast field generated by an object approximately fourteen kilometres below the northern impact basin. NTO-312, Hynox, and the Lyoes may be separate responses to the same carrier signal. No Agent or Head Xenobiologist is authorised to know that the signal has begun answering our probes.',date:'PRIME // 001',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'OVERSEER DIRECTIVE: Preserve Noro Castellun until the BLACK CROWN chamber is open.'},
{id:402,type:'overseer',tag:'ONYX CHANNEL // SEALED ORDER',title:'Contingency: WHITE SILENCE',summary:'Final containment protocol if ASOA-203 contamination reaches an Osprey.',body:'If any extraction craft returns a positive Leoyn or Hynox reading after orbital ascent, WHITE SILENCE is authorised. Remote-lock the craft, erase navigation records, and redirect it into the system star. Crew recovery is prohibited regardless of identity or clearance.',date:'PRIME // 002',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'The first contaminated Osprey has already left ASOA-203. Its current location is [[CLASSIFIED]].'},
{id:501,type:'specops',tag:'SPECIAL OPS // PLANETFALL',title:'Operation DEAD STAR',summary:'A massive strike into the Radiation Storm to seize the BLACK CROWN signal source.',body:`OBSIDIAN COMMAND // EXTINCTION-LEVEL OPERATION

OBJECTIVE
Deploy three Cargo Ospreys, twenty-four autonomous gun platforms, and every cleared Special Operations unit into the northern impact basin. Breach fourteen kilometres beneath ASOA-203 and secure the BLACK CROWN chamber.

PHASE I — SKYBREAK
Orbital batteries create a ninety-second corridor through the storm. Osprey One deploys gravity anchors. Osprey Two delivers assault teams. Osprey Three acts as an unmanned contamination decoy.

PHASE II — DEEP KNIFE
Obsidian teams descend through the impact bore while drones hold every junction. Prayer nests are bypassed. Warden contact authorises antimatter breaching charges.

PHASE III — CROWN SEIZURE
Establish a null field around the signal object. No voice, image, or command from inside the chamber is trusted—even with Overseer authentication.

FAILURE CONDITION
Activate the Dead Star payload and remove the northern hemisphere from the operational map.`,date:'T-MINUS 72H',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'Noro Castellun has not been informed that DEAD STAR includes his termination order.'},
{id:502,type:'specops',tag:'SPECIAL OPS // ARMORY',title:'Obsidian Arsenal',summary:'Restricted weapons authorised only for extinction-level operations.',body:`MASS-DRIVER LANCE — Penetrates Throne cores and Warden columns.

GRAVITON CAGE — Pins airborne Prayers and crushes baseline infected inside a twelve-metre field.

SUNSPIKE CHARGE — Miniature fusion lance used for deep-site breaching.

NULL CHOIR HELMET — Replaces external sound with tactical data to resist Cantor influence.

LAST-LIGHT IMPLANT — Transmits an operator’s final sensory record, then destroys all biological material inside the suit.`,date:'ARSENAL // OBSIDIAN',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'Last-Light can be activated remotely by the Overseer.'},
{id:503,type:'specops',tag:'SPECIAL OPS // KILL TEAM',title:'Unit NIGHTFALL',summary:'The Directorate’s highest-clearance strike team for impossible recoveries.',body:`NIGHTFALL-1 // COMMAND
Coordinates orbital support and overrides all field Agents.

NIGHTFALL-2 // BREACHER
Carries the Mass-Driver Lance and powered siege frame.

NIGHTFALL-3 // VEIL
Uses experimental nonlocal phase armour.

NIGHTFALL-4 // CINDER
May sterilise entire facilities without additional approval.

NIGHTFALL-5 // WRAITH
No biological profile exists. Identity is sealed even from Head Xenobiologist clearance.

DIRECTIVE
NIGHTFALL retrieves objectives, destroys evidence, and leaves no viable infection behind.`,date:'UNIT // ACTIVE',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-4',hx:'NIGHTFALL-5 may be the original ASOA-203 humanoid recovered before Patient Zero.'},
