{id:701,type:'lore',tag:'TRAINING LOG // SESSION 01',title:'Radiation Storm Acclimation',summary:'Agents enter a simulated storm corridor while respirator systems progressively fail.',body:`INSTRUCTOR: CAPTAIN SERA VALE\n\nThe squad crossed a 400-metre simulated contamination corridor with visibility reduced to two metres. At minute six, respirator warnings were introduced. Vesper maintained rear coverage while Forge restored the relay beacons. Razor broke formation twice and received a formal correction.\n\nTRAINING RESULT\nFive of six Agents reached extraction within the required window. Echo completed the route unseen and was waiting inside the recovery Osprey before the exercise officially ended.\n\nRECOMMENDATION\nRepeat under live radiation conditions before Operation Blacklight Hypothermia begins.`,date:'TRAINING // 01',threat:'CLEARANCE: AGENT',hx:'The simulated warning at minute six matched a real Hynox exposure. Agents were not informed.'},
{id:702,type:'lore',tag:'TRAINING LOG // SESSION 02',title:'Prayer Ambush Drill',summary:'A live-fire exercise teaches the squad to survive coordinated pouncing attacks.',body:`LOCATION: VERTICAL COMBAT CHAMBER 4\n\nSix mechanical Prayer frames were positioned above a ruined urban course. Agents were required to maintain overlapping sight lines while transporting a weighted casualty. Bulwark intercepted four pounces. Solace stabilised the casualty without stopping the formation.\n\nTRAINING RESULT\nRazor destroyed a frame before it entered the marked engagement zone. Vesper disabled the final unit through three layers of moving cover.\n\nFAILURE NOTE\nEvery Agent looked upward during the first audio lure, leaving ground-level access unobserved.`,date:'TRAINING // 02',threat:'CLEARANCE: AGENT',hx:'The seventh movement detected in the chamber was not part of the exercise.'},
{id:703,type:'lore',tag:'TRAINING LOG // SESSION 03',title:'Cargo Osprey Emergency Descent',summary:'Agents rehearse orbital insertion after navigation and lift systems are disabled.',body:`AIRFRAME: OSPREY C-19\n\nAt 18,000 metres, instructors disabled automated navigation, one lift engine, and internal lighting. Forge rerouted cargo power while Vesper calculated a manual descent corridor. Bulwark secured the cabin against decompression.\n\nTRAINING RESULT\nHard landing completed inside the target radius. Simulated casualties: two. Cargo survival: eighty-seven percent.\n\nINSTRUCTOR NOTE\nEcho left the aircraft before touchdown and activated the landing beacon from the ground. No authorised exit was recorded.`,date:'TRAINING // 03',threat:'CLEARANCE: AGENT',hx:'C-19 received a BLACK CROWN transmission during descent. Audio has been moved to Corbius.'},
{id:704,type:'directive',tag:'INTRODUCTION // FIELD PREPARATION',title:'Before Planetfall',summary:'Required preparation sequence for every Agent assigned to ASOA-203.',body:`SEVENTY-TWO HOURS BEFORE INSERTION\nComplete Hynox baseline screening and seal all personal communications.\n\nTWENTY-FOUR HOURS BEFORE INSERTION\nReceive mission respirator, three MRE packs, three Aquabottles, radiation tabs, and assigned class equipment.\n\nONE HOUR BEFORE INSERTION\nMemorise the current challenge phrase. Destroy all written copies. Confirm that no unfamiliar voice is present on squad communications.\n\nAT PLANETFALL\nDo not remove the respirator. Do not answer voices outside visual range. Do not follow anyone who claims the mission has been cancelled.`,date:'MANDATORY',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-2',hx:'There is no approved mission-cancellation phrase.'},
{id:711,type:'corbiusops',tag:'CORBIUS // PLANETFALL ROUTE',title:'Insertion Corridor: GRAVEGLASS',summary:'True mission route from orbital staging to the BLACK CROWN excavation zone.',body:`PRIMARY DESTINATION\nNorthern Impact Basin, ASOA-203\nCoordinates: 44.091 N / 17.203 E\n\nINSERTION\nCargo Osprey C-19 enters beneath Storm Layer Seven using a six-second orbital blind spot. Agents deploy at Relay Graveglass, then travel north through the buried mag-rail for 31 kilometres.\n\nWAYPOINTS\n1. Relay Graveglass — restore the underground navigation lattice.\n2. Saint Mercy Annex — recover Pathogen Case NTO-312/IX.\n3. Calder Transit Spine — cross beneath the active Prayer migration route.\n4. Borehole K-0 — descend to the BLACK CROWN chamber.\n\nEXTRACTION\nThere is no scheduled Osprey recovery. Agents must activate the pre-outbreak mass elevator at K-0.`,date:'CORBIUS // ROUTE 01',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'The Agents have been told an Osprey will retrieve them. This is false.'},
{id:712,type:'corbiusops',tag:'CORBIUS // MISSION TRUTH',title:'Actual Objective: NINTH CHOIR',summary:'Operation Blacklight Hypothermia is not an extermination mission.',body:`PUBLIC OBJECTIVE\nExterminate infected, locate survivors, and recover NTO-312 Generation IX.\n\nACTUAL OBJECTIVE\nUse the six Agent implants as a distributed key to open the BLACK CROWN chamber. Each class system contains one section of the activation sequence. The Agents were selected for equipment compatibility, not survival probability.\n\nSUCCESS CONDITION\nThe chamber opens and transmits a complete NINTH CHOIR signal to the Corbius orbital receiver.\n\nACCEPTABLE LOSSES\nAll field personnel. All AEGIS facilities on ASOA-203. Northern continental population.`,date:'CORBIUS // OBJECTIVE',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'Noro Castellun may abort the activation only before the fifth Agent key connects.'},
{id:713,type:'corbiusops',tag:'CORBIUS // SITE MAP',title:'Destination File: Borehole K-0',summary:'A classified descent map for the final mission location.',body:`DEPTH 0–2 KM // DEAD CITY\nDense zombified population. No orbital support.\n\nDEPTH 2–6 KM // LYOE GALLERIES\nPrayer migration shafts and at least two dormant Thrones.\n\nDEPTH 6–10 KM // HUMAN FACILITY\nArchitecture matches no registered AEGIS construction, yet carries Directorate serial numbers dated 140 years before AEGIS existed.\n\nDEPTH 10–14 KM // SIGNAL OCEAN\nGravity fluctuates. Radio messages arrive before they are transmitted.\n\nDEPTH 14.2 KM // BLACK CROWN\nNo physical map survives below this point.`,date:'CORBIUS // K-0',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'The Head Xenobiologist’s key-shaped insignia is identical to the K-0 chamber lock.'},
{id:721,type:'corbiusintel',tag:'CORBIUS // ORIGIN',title:'The First AEGIS',summary:'Evidence that the Directorate has been rebuilt multiple times.',body:`Recovered K-0 records identify seven organisations named AEGIS across a period of 2,400 years. Each was founded independently after receiving the same dream: an eye inside a key.\n\nEvery AEGIS eventually discovered ASOA-203. Every AEGIS opened the chamber. Every AEGIS disappeared from historical record within one year.\n\nCorbius was created to observe the cycle without becoming part of it.`,date:'CORBIUS // HISTORY',threat:'CLASSIFICATION: SOVEREIGN',hx:'Noro Castellun is the first Head Xenobiologist to discover the pattern before chamber activation.'},
{id:722,type:'corbiusintel',tag:'CORBIUS // AGENT ASSESSMENT',title:'Predicted Agent Survival',summary:'Corbius projections for the Graveglass insertion team.',body:`VESPER — 31% probability of reaching K-0.\nRAZOR — 18% probability; highest projected Lyoe elimination count.\nSOLACE — 44% probability; primary target of the Throne network.\nFORGE — 52% probability; required to operate the mass elevator.\nECHO — Result unavailable. Predictive systems cannot locate her after Borehole Level Six.\nBULWARK — 9% probability; death predicted while holding the final chamber approach.\n\nFULL TEAM EXTRACTION PROBABILITY: 0.7%`,date:'CORBIUS // FORECAST',threat:'CLASSIFICATION: SOVEREIGN',hx:'Do not allow Agents access to individual projections.'},
{id:723,type:'corbiuspathogen',tag:'CORBIUS // PATHOGEN',title:'NTO-312 Generation IX',summary:'The virus is a communications medium, not a biological weapon.',body:`NTO-312 builds microscopic receiving structures inside dead neural tissue. Zombified humanoids are antennae in a planetary network. Hynox prepares living tissue for reception. Leoyn allows Lyoes to transmit instructions through infected hosts.\n\nGeneration IX does not spread faster than previous samples. It listens farther.\n\nIf carried into orbit, a single infected body could connect BLACK CROWN to every inhabited system using Osprey navigation relays.`,date:'CORBIUS // BIOHAZARD',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'The pathogen sample requested by the mission is already aboard Osprey C-19.'},
{id:731,type:'corbiuslogs',tag:'CORBIUS // SEALED LOG',title:'Training Session Zero',summary:'A training session none of the Agents remember attending.',body:`DATE: 184 DAYS BEFORE RECRUITMENT\n\nAll six Agents entered Chamber 12 voluntarily. None had met before. A BLACK CROWN fragment was activated for eleven seconds. Each subject spoke the same coordinates, then selected the equipment class they would later receive.\n\nMemory removal succeeded in five subjects. Echo retained partial awareness and has been pretending otherwise.\n\nAt the end of the session, a seventh voice said: “Bring them home.”`,date:'CORBIUS // LOG 00',threat:'CLASSIFICATION: SOVEREIGN',hx:'Noro Castellun supervised Session Zero but has no memory of being present.'},
{id:732,type:'corbiuslogs',tag:'CORBIUS // SEALED LOG',title:'Osprey C-19 Black Box',summary:'The aircraft completed the mission before it was assigned.',body:`BLACK BOX TIMESTAMP: 19 DAYS IN THE FUTURE\n\nC-19 emerges from the Radiation Storm with no crew aboard. Cargo mass indicates seven passengers. Interior cameras show empty seats. The flight computer repeatedly requests docking permission using Overseer credentials.\n\nFinal transmission:\n“Graveglass complete. Crown open. We brought back the sky.”`,date:'CORBIUS // PARADOX',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'Current C-19 black-box serial number matches the recovered future device.'},
{id:733,type:'corbiuslogs',tag:'CORBIUS // TERMINATION ORDER',title:'WHITE SILENCE Authority',summary:'Conditions under which the entire operation must be erased.',body:`WHITE SILENCE activates if any of the following occur:\n\n• BLACK CROWN addresses an Agent by their birth name.\n• Echo appears in two locations simultaneously.\n• Noro Castellun removes the eye-key insignia.\n• Osprey C-19 requests docking before mission completion.\n• An Agent reports blue sky beneath Borehole Level Ten.\n\nUpon activation, Corbius assumes command, terminates all AEGIS communications, and sterilises ASOA-203 from orbit.`,date:'CORBIUS // FINAL',threat:'AUTHORITY: ABSOLUTE',hx:'Overseer authorisation is not required once a trigger is confirmed.'},
{id:724,type:'corbiuspathogen',tag:'CORBIUS PATHOGEN // INTERACTION',title:'Cross-Infection: Hynox + Leoyn',summary:'Dual infection creates an organism capable of receiving and transmitting BLACK CROWN commands.',body:`When Hynox conductive growth and Leoyn adaptive tissue exist in one host, both illnesses accelerate. The host becomes a two-way relay capable of receiving BLACK CROWN instructions and transmitting them directly to nearby Lyoes.

GAMEPLAY EFFECTS
Maximum HP falls by 10 after every long rest. At the beginning of each encounter, the Overseer may reposition one Lyoe before initiative. Healing the host restores the same amount of HP to the nearest Lyoe within 60 feet.

IDENTIFICATION
The subject casts two shadows under a single light source. Radio equipment repeats their heartbeat. Prayer organisms refuse to pounce on them.

CONTAINMENT
No treatment is approved. White Silence authority is automatic if a dual-infected host reaches orbit.`,date:'CORBIUS // INTERACTION',threat:'BIOHAZARD: ONYX-5',hx:'Subject H-19 may be the only stable dual-infected humanoid.'},
{id:725,type:'corbiuspathogen',tag:'CORBIUS PATHOGEN // SCREENING',title:'Field Infection Checks',summary:'Gameplay procedure for testing Agents after exposure.',body:`WHEN TO TEST
After entering storm rain, receiving Lyoe damage, removing a respirator, touching infected tissue, or completing a mission sector.

HYNOX CHECK
Roll 1d20 plus equipment protection. Difficulty 13 in weak radiation, 16 inside the storm, and 19 near BLACK CROWN.

LEOYN CHECK
Roll 1d20 plus medical protection. Difficulty equals 10 plus the source Lyoe’s ONYX level.

FAILED CHECK
Mark one infection stage. A natural 1 advances two stages. A natural 20 prevents infection and grants advantage on the next check against the same source.

MEDICAL SCREENING
Solace or an HX laboratory can identify the stage. Ordinary scanners produce a false negative during the first hour.`,date:'CORBIUS // FIELD RULES',threat:'PROTOCOL: MANDATORY',hx:'The Overseer may secretly record failed checks until symptoms become visible.'},
{id:726,type:'corbiuspathogen',tag:'CORBIUS PATHOGEN // COUNTERMEASURES',title:'Experimental Treatments',summary:'Restricted countermeasures capable of delaying infection at severe cost.',body:`RAD-TAB K-11
Delays Hynox progression for 1d6 hours. Repeated use deals 2d6 damage to the user.

WHITE-SALT INJECTION
Allows a new Leoyn check with advantage during Stage I. Failure immediately advances to Stage II.

SYNTHETIC BLOOD PURGE
Solace may spend three drone charges to reduce either infection by one stage. The patient permanently loses 1d10 maximum HP.

NULL-FIELD EXPOSURE
Pauses all symptoms for ten minutes. When the field ends, roll 1d20. On 10 or lower, every paused stage activates simultaneously.

HX PROTOCOL CASTELLUN
A classified treatment derived from Noro Castellun’s blood. One stored dose exists. Results on ordinary humans are unknown.`,date:'CORBIUS // TREATMENT',threat:'CLASSIFICATION: SOVEREIGN',hx:'Protocol Castellun may cure both infections—or complete the receiver structure instantly.'},
{id:801,type:'research',tag:'XENO RESEARCH // SUBJECT K-27',title:'Subject K-27 — Choirskin',summary:'A humanoid test subject whose skin converts nearby sound into physical vibration.',body:`RESEARCH OBJECTIVE
Determine whether Cantor signal tissue can be integrated into a living human without full Leoyn conversion.

PROCEDURE
K-27 received six cultivated filament grafts along the spine. Within forty-eight hours, the subject’s skin began vibrating in response to speech and radio traffic.

OBSERVED EFFECTS
Whispered words create visible ripples across the body. Loud sounds produce concussive force. During Trial 11, K-27 repeated a Cantor hymn without opening their mouth and shattered the observation window.

CONTAINMENT
The chamber must remain acoustically isolated. Personnel communicate through text terminals only. If K-27 begins vibrating without an external sound source, evacuate the research wing.

STATUS
Alive. Cooperative. Claims another voice is practising inside their bones.`,date:'TRIAL // K-27',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-3',hx:'K-27 can hear Corbius communications despite complete network isolation.'},
{id:802,type:'research',tag:'XENO RESEARCH // SUBJECT M-04',title:'Subject M-04 — Borrowed Face',summary:'A regenerative humanoid that grows the facial features of anyone whose blood it touches.',body:`RESEARCH OBJECTIVE
Develop rapid tissue replacement using Weeper mimic structures.

PROCEDURE
Synthetic Weeper cells were introduced into a deceased test body. M-04 regained circulation after nine minutes and requested a mirror.

OBSERVED EFFECTS
Blood contact causes M-04 to copy facial structure, fingerprints, voice, and fragments of recent memory. The copied identity remains for approximately six hours. Multiple samples cause features to overlap unpredictably.

CONTAINMENT
No exposed skin is permitted inside the chamber. Staff must confirm identity through rotating challenge phrases. M-04 is not allowed to view Agent personnel files.

STATUS
Containment uncertain. Three technicians now claim to be the original M-04.`,date:'TRIAL // M-04',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-4',hx:'One technician passed HX biometric verification using Noro Castellun’s blood profile.'},
{id:803,type:'research',tag:'XENO RESEARCH // SUBJECT A-12',title:'Subject A-12 — Zero Gravity Host',summary:'A humanoid altered to survive where the Radiation Storm reverses local gravity.',body:`RESEARCH OBJECTIVE
Create a viable scout for the inverted-gravity zones surrounding Borehole K-0.

PROCEDURE
A-12 received vestibular implants, reinforced organs, and controlled exposure to storm particles during orbital freefall.

OBSERVED EFFECTS
The subject can choose the direction in which their body experiences gravity. Nearby unsecured objects occasionally follow. A-12 sleeps suspended against the chamber ceiling and insists that “down” points toward BLACK CROWN.

FIELD VALUE
A-12 could cross collapsed shafts inaccessible to ordinary Agents and carry a navigation line through Signal Ocean.

STATUS
Physically stable. Psychological orientation deteriorating.`,date:'TRIAL // A-12',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-2',hx:'A-12 points toward BLACK CROWN even when transported off-world.'},
{id:804,type:'research',tag:'XENO RESEARCH // SUBJECT R-31',title:'Subject R-31 — Dead Relay',summary:'A clinically dead humanoid that continues transmitting tactical information.',body:`RESEARCH OBJECTIVE
Test whether NTO-312 can preserve useful cognition after biological death.

PROCEDURE
R-31 volunteered for controlled infection and was declared dead at 03:14. Brain activity ended. At 03:19, every terminal in the laboratory displayed the subject’s personnel number.

OBSERVED EFFECTS
R-31 communicates through nearby electronics, correctly predicts infected movement, and remembers conversations held after death. The body remains motionless, but new fingerprints appear on the inside of the containment glass.

CONTAINMENT
Disconnecting power does not stop transmission. No device that receives R-31 is permitted to connect to an Osprey.

STATUS
Deceased. Active.`,date:'TRIAL // R-31',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-4',hx:'R-31 claims to be speaking from inside the future C-19 black box.'},
{id:805,type:'research',tag:'XENO RESEARCH // SUBJECT S-08',title:'Subject S-08 — Sunless Child',summary:'A juvenile humanoid recovered alive from fourteen kilometres beneath ASOA-203.',body:`RECOVERY
S-08 was found outside the sealed BLACK CROWN chamber before any AEGIS expedition reached Borehole K-0. The subject appeared human, carried no equipment, and showed no radiation damage.

OBSERVED EFFECTS
S-08 does not sleep, eat, age, or cast a shadow. Lyoes become passive within twenty metres. Zombies kneel and face away from the subject.

INTERVIEW
S-08 speaks every language in the archive but answers only one question: “Are we home yet?”

CONTAINMENT
The chamber lights must never be fully extinguished. During the single blackout event, S-08 moved through six sealed doors without opening them.

STATUS
Calm. Waiting.`,date:'SUBJECT // S-08',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'S-08 calls Noro Castellun “the last key.”'},
{id:806,type:'research',tag:'XENO RESEARCH // PROJECT',title:'Project Second Breath',summary:'An attempt to reverse zombification while preserving the original human mind.',body:`OBJECTIVE
Remove NTO-312 control structures from an infected brain without destroying retained consciousness.

METHOD
A captured Shambler is placed inside a null-field while Seraph drones remove crystal growth from the brain stem. Synthetic blood restores circulation as the signal connection collapses.

RESULTS
Trials 1–18 ended in immediate death. Trial 19 restored speech for ninety seconds. The subject identified family members, requested water, and warned that the infection could still see through their eyes.

CURRENT TRIAL
Subject H-19 remains conscious and responsive. Removal is delayed because the organism now occupies tissue required for memory and movement.

ETHICAL STATUS
Suspended by AEGIS. Continued under HX authority.`,date:'PROJECT // ACTIVE',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-3',hx:'H-19 has asked HX to stop trying. The request has not been entered into the official trial log.'},
{id:811,type:'overseer',tag:'ONYX CHANNEL // EXECUTIVE ORDER',title:'Directive ONYX-0: Chain of Command',summary:'The true command hierarchy for Operation Blacklight Hypothermia.',body:`AUTHORITY ORDER
1. Overseer Onyx Prime
2. Corbius Sovereign System
3. Special Operations Obsidian Command
4. Head Xenobiologist Noro Castellun
5. Field Agent command structure

OVERRIDE CONDITIONS
The Overseer may assume direct control of any Osprey, Agent implant, defence platform, or research containment system without local approval.

CONFLICT PROTOCOL
If Corbius and Onyx Prime issue contradictory orders, obey the order carrying the later timestamp. If timestamps match, terminate the communication relay and await WHITE SILENCE.

DISCLOSURE
No person below Special Operations clearance is permitted to know that Corbius appears in the hierarchy.`,date:'ONYX // ORDER 00',threat:'AUTHORITY: ABSOLUTE',hx:'Noro Castellun has repeatedly rejected this chain of command.'},
{id:812,type:'overseer',tag:'ONYX CHANNEL // ASSET CONTROL',title:'Agent Implant Backdoors',summary:'Hidden command functions installed inside every Agent class system.',body:`VESPER
Coldstar optic can be remotely blinded or redirected to a designated target.

RAZOR
Kestrel frame can lock all joints and administer its complete stimulant reserve.

SOLACE
Seraph drones can prioritise specimen recovery over human treatment.

FORGE
Helix may classify its operator as hostile infrastructure.

ECHO
Phase-mesh recall signal can force re-entry at an unknown location.

BULWARK
Atlas harness can reverse its gravity field and immobilise the wearer.

AUTHORITY
These functions require Onyx Prime clearance. Agents were not informed during equipment consent.`,date:'ONYX // ASSETS',threat:'CLASSIFICATION: PRIME',hx:'HX can disable one backdoor permanently, but doing so alerts the Overseer.'},
{id:813,type:'overseer',tag:'ONYX CHANNEL // ORBITAL',title:'Sterilisation Platform HELIOS',summary:'An orbital weapon positioned above ASOA-203 under sole Overseer authority.',body:`PLATFORM
HELIOS carries twelve focused fusion lances and a planet-facing mass driver. It is disguised as a weather-monitoring satellite.

CAPABILITY
One lance can sterilise a ten-kilometre site. All twelve can ignite the upper Radiation Storm and remove viable surface life across the northern hemisphere.

ACTIVATION
ONYX-PRIME authorisation followed by a thirty-second biometric hold. Corbius may bypass the hold under WHITE SILENCE conditions.

LIMITATION
BLACK CROWN interference creates a six-minute blind period during each orbit. Graveglass insertion is scheduled inside this gap.

CURRENT STATE
Armed. Tracking Osprey C-19.`,date:'ONYX // HELIOS',threat:'THREAT: EXTINCTION',hx:'HELIOS targeting includes every known AEGIS installation, including off-world laboratories.'},
{id:814,type:'overseer',tag:'ONYX CHANNEL // SUCCESSION',title:'If Onyx Prime Is Compromised',summary:'Automatic succession and termination instructions for the highest clearance.',body:`COMPROMISE INDICATORS
• Onyx Prime requests access to raw BLACK CROWN audio.
• Two valid Overseer orders arrive from different locations.
• The Overseer refers to ASOA-203 as “home.”
• Biometric scans show Hynox crystal growth.

RESPONSE
Obsidian Command isolates all executive relays. HX performs a silent pathogen test. If compromise is confirmed, NIGHTFALL-5 executes the Overseer and destroys the Onyx credential core.

SUCCESSION
No human successor is appointed. Corbius assumes temporary control until a new Onyx Prime is selected from outside the AEGIS Directorate.

FINAL CHECK
The current Overseer has failed one compromise indicator. Investigation remains sealed.`,date:'ONYX // SUCCESSION',threat:'CLASSIFICATION: PRIME',hx:'The failed indicator was the use of the word “home.”'},
{id:815,type:'overseer',tag:'ONYX CHANNEL // OBSERVATION',title:'Noro Castellun Contingency',summary:'Surveillance and containment plan for the Head Xenobiologist.',body:`RISK
Noro Castellun’s biology interferes with Hynox, matches the BLACK CROWN lock, and appears throughout records predating his birth.

OBSERVATION
All HX authoring activity is mirrored to the ONYX Channel. Interviews involving S-08 are monitored without the knowledge of local staff.

CONTINGENCY CASTELLUN
If Noro attempts to leave ASOA-203 before chamber activation, disable his transport and transfer him to NIGHTFALL custody. If he removes the eye-key insignia, activate WHITE SILENCE immediately.

PROHIBITION
Do not kill Noro before the chamber opens. Previous cycles suggest his death causes another individual to assume the same biological signature within seventy-two hours.`,date:'ONYX // SUBJECT HX',threat:'THREAT: ONYX-5',hx:'This file is visible to HX only if Corbius deliberately exposes it.'}
